	doi = {10.1111/j.1365-2125.1986.tb02823.x},
	abstract = {The pharmacokinetics of enalaprilat were studied after administration of single and multiple doses of enalapril maleate to people with normal and impaired renal  function. Renal impairment was associated with higher serum concentrations of  enalaprilat, longer times to peak concentrations, slower decline of serum  concentrations and with reduced urinary elimination. Urinary elimination of  enalaprilat was closely related to renal function. In patients with severe renal  impairment ({GFR} values below 30 ml min-1 1.73 m-2) significantly smaller doses of  enalapril maleate will be required than in patients with normal or less severely  impaired renal function.},
