	abstract = {A cross over single and multiple dose study was carried out to find out pharmacokinetic interactions between diphynylhydantoin ({DPH}) (35 mg/kg, p.o.) and  antihypertensives enalapril (1.6 mg/kg; p.o.) and amlodipine (0.4 mg/kg, p.o.) in  rhesus monkeys. Neither the plasma concentrations nor the pharmacokinetic  parameters of {DPH} were altered by coadministration of enalapril or amlodipine,  suggesting that enalapril and amlodipine can be safely administered to epileptic  patients receiving phenytoin.},
